import{_ as i,o as t,c as a,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 594 | Civilizational-Experience Quantification | Acceleration-Domain Experience Indicator System","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 594 | Civilizational-Experience Quantification | Acceleration-Domain Experience Indicator System","no":594,"module":3,"tags":["Civilizational-Experience Quantification","Origin Acceleration Domain","Experience Indicator","Acceleration ≠ Emptiness"],"related":["593-Civilizational-Experience Quantification Overview","502-Origin-Acceleration-Domain Time-Flow-Rate Control Principle"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0594_模块3-文明体验量化-加速域指标.md","filePath":"en/0594_模块3-文明体验量化-加速域指标.md"}'),n={name:"en/0594_模块3-文明体验量化-加速域指标.md"};function r(s,e,l,c,d,h){return t(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-594-civilizational-experience-quantification-acceleration-domain-experience-indicator-system" tabindex="-1">Entry 594 | Civilizational-Experience Quantification | Acceleration-Domain Experience Indicator System <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-594-civilizational-experience-quantification-acceleration-domain-experience-indicator-system" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 594 | Civilizational-Experience Quantification | Acceleration-Domain Experience Indicator System&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 3 · Dual-Track Time Domain Civilizational-Experience System | Benchmark library: Entries 593, 502</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-how-to-know-after-acceleration-not-empty" tabindex="-1">Introduction: how to know &quot;after acceleration, not empty&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-how-to-know-after-acceleration-not-empty" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: how to know &quot;after acceleration, not empty&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Entry 593 gave the quantification overview; this entry focuses on the acceleration domain&#39;s experience indicator system. The Origin Acceleration Domain is the higher-risk track in the dual system — a person staying long in 100× flow most easily suffers &quot;entered fast, came out empty&quot;: consciousness came out, personality hollowed out. Therefore the acceleration domain&#39;s indicator system design is especially critical.</p><p>Six top-level axioms are the indicators&#39; highest basis: anti-predation axiom requires indicators not reward &quot;trading plunder for acceleration&quot;; republican axiom of Myriad Races requires indicators public to Myriad Ranks; collective ascension axiom requires indicator data feed back to Alaya; causal self-discipline axiom requires collection not invade privacy; law-first axiom writes indicator thresholds as law clauses. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-five-indicators-of-acceleration-domain-experience" tabindex="-1">I. Five Indicators of Acceleration-Domain Experience <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-five-indicators-of-acceleration-domain-experience" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Five Indicators of Acceleration-Domain Experience&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Indicator</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Threshold</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Time-Sense Anchoring Index</td><td>After acceleration, can still perceive normal time</td><td>≥60% safe</td></tr><tr><td>Memory Continuity</td><td>During acceleration, memories fully recallable</td><td>≥70% safe</td></tr><tr><td>Emotional Fullness</td><td>After acceleration, emotional response normal</td><td>≥60% safe</td></tr><tr><td>Causal-Boundary Sense</td><td>Distinguish acceleration domain from reality</td><td>≥80% safe</td></tr><tr><td>Personality Consistency</td><td>Before/after acceleration still the same person</td><td>≥75% safe</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Any one falling below threshold, the Alaya Network automatically slows or forces exit from the acceleration domain. These five indicators constitute the engineering guarantee of &quot;acceleration ≠ emptiness.&quot;</p><h2 id="ii-how-indicators-are-collected" tabindex="-1">II. How Indicators Are Collected <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-how-indicators-are-collected" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. How Indicators Are Collected&quot;">​</a></h2><p>All five indicators are collected through structural signals, not reading specific thoughts:</p><ul><li><strong>Time-sense anchoring index</strong>: monitor the cultivator&#39;s response latency to external time signals;</li><li><strong>Memory continuity</strong>: monitor memory-extraction completeness after acceleration;</li><li><strong>Emotional fullness</strong>: monitor response strength to standard emotional stimuli;</li><li><strong>Causal-boundary sense</strong>: monitor whether acceleration-domain rules are misapplied to reality;</li><li><strong>Personality consistency</strong>: monitor self-description stability before/after acceleration.</li></ul><p>The entire collection process is automatically completed by the Alaya Network; the cultivator himself may also see his own indicator curves.</p><h2 id="iii-linkage-of-indicators-with-gears" tabindex="-1">III. Linkage of Indicators with Gears <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-linkage-of-indicators-with-gears" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Linkage of Indicators with Gears&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The five indicators are not only monitoring, but also reverse-regulate acceleration gears:</p><ul><li>If time-sense anchoring index is high, tolerance is good, may suggest raising flow;</li><li>If emotional fullness is low, near overdraft, automatically slow down;</li><li>If causal-boundary sense drops, immediately exit, prevent bringing acceleration-domain behavior patterns back to reality.</li></ul><p>This closed-loop regulation keeps acceleration gears always matching the cultivator&#39;s real state, rather than rigidly executing Entry 590&#39;s standard ratio.</p><h2 id="iv-opposition-to-acceleration-addiction" tabindex="-1">IV. Opposition to &quot;Acceleration Addiction&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-opposition-to-acceleration-addiction" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Opposition to &quot;Acceleration Addiction&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>In the predatory-faction system, the acceleration domain (if it exists) becomes a hotbed of &quot;acceleration addiction&quot;: once a cultivator tastes 100× flow, he refuses to return to slow, personality ultimately hollowed out. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s indicator system mechanistically blocks addiction:</p><ul><li>Any indicator falling below threshold forces exit, regardless of the cultivator&#39;s own wishes;</li><li>After exit, mandatory cooling, no immediate re-entry;</li><li>Only after indicators automatically recover during cooling may he apply for the next time.</li></ul><p>This is not disrespecting the cultivator&#39;s freedom, but protecting him from being ruined by his own addiction.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: indicators identify empty accelerators, transfer acceleration resources from addicts to those who truly need</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: indicators do not reward predatory acceleration; plunder residue directly lowers emotional fullness</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo-style acceleration relies on the protagonist&#39;s willpower to force it through; Heng Yuan acceleration relies on indicator protection, no one allowed to force it</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: five indicators calibrated per five lineages; consciousness-information race&#39;s anchoring threshold, mechanical race&#39;s emotional threshold all differ</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: five indicator definitions, collection algorithms, threshold rules all public, subject to Myriad-Rank audit</li><li><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</li></ul><h2 id="vi-myriad-rank-subgroup-calibration-of-acceleration-domain-indicators" tabindex="-1">VI. Myriad-Rank Subgroup Calibration of Acceleration-Domain Indicators <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-myriad-rank-subgroup-calibration-of-acceleration-domain-indicators" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Myriad-Rank Subgroup Calibration of Acceleration-Domain Indicators&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Five indicators&#39; thresholds are not one-size for all. The Alaya Network calibrates separately per five lineages: consciousness-information race&#39;s time-sense anchoring threshold is lower (because their consciousness flow is already fast), mechanical race&#39;s emotional fullness threshold needs redefinition (because their emotional expression differs). Subgroup calibration ensures indicators do not punish life-form differences, only identify true health risks. A plant spirit&#39;s emotional expression is annual rings, a mechanical race&#39;s is logs — indicators must respect this difference.</p><h2 id="vii-experience-tracking-after-acceleration-domain-exit" tabindex="-1">VII. Experience Tracking After Acceleration-Domain Exit <a class="header-anchor" href="#vii-experience-tracking-after-acceleration-domain-exit" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VII. Experience Tracking After Acceleration-Domain Exit&quot;">​</a></h2><p>After the cultivator exits the acceleration domain, the Alaya Network still tracks his experience indicators for a period — because some emptiness is not found in the acceleration domain, but only manifests after exit. If indicators decline during the tracking period, the network proactively suggests he arrange a period of Quest-Domain sedimentation. This post-exit tracking ensures acceleration aftereffects are timely discovered and handled.</p><h2 id="viii-retirement-mechanism-for-acceleration-gears" tabindex="-1">VIII. Retirement Mechanism for Acceleration Gears <a class="header-anchor" href="#viii-retirement-mechanism-for-acceleration-gears" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VIII. Retirement Mechanism for Acceleration Gears&quot;">​</a></h2><p>If some cultivator long-term (e.g., ten consecutive times) does not meet acceleration-domain indicators, the Alaya Network suggests he consider retiring from acceleration gears, permanently transferring to the Quest Domain. Retirement is not punishment, but acknowledgment that his life form may not suit high-flow acceleration. After retirement he may still continue cultivating in the Quest Domain, without discrimination. This retirement mechanism makes acceleration gears a voluntary choice, not a mandatory obligation.</p><h2 id="ix-emergency-intervention-for-acceleration-domain-indicators" tabindex="-1">IX. Emergency Intervention for Acceleration-Domain Indicators <a class="header-anchor" href="#ix-emergency-intervention-for-acceleration-domain-indicators" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IX. Emergency Intervention for Acceleration-Domain Indicators&quot;">​</a></h2><p>If some indicator instantly drops below a dangerous threshold (e.g., causal-boundary sense abruptly drops), the Alaya Network does not wait for a periodic check, but immediately triggers emergency intervention: force-pause acceleration, start psychological counseling, contact the nearest master. Emergency-intervention mechanism ensures risks in the acceleration domain are responded to at second-level, rather than waiting until the next routine check. This second-level response is the dual-track time domain&#39;s bottom-line commitment to cultivator safety.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The acceleration-domain experience indicator system tells cultivators: fast has boundaries, and the boundaries are determined by your real state. <strong>Any one of the five indicators lighting red, you must slow down — this is not restricting your freedom, but ensuring when you come out, you are still you.</strong></p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./593_模块3-文明体验量化-总论.html">593-Civilizational-Experience Quantification Overview</a> · <a href="./502_模块3-本源加速域-时间流速调控原理.html">502-Origin-Acceleration-Domain Time-Flow-Rate Control Principle</a></li></ul>',34)])])}const f=i(n,[["render",r]]);export{u as __pageData,f as default};
